# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body — explain WHY, not WHAT; wrap at 72 chars>
#
# <footer>
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Conventional Commits cheat sheet:
#
#   types:    feat | fix | refactor | chore | docs | style |
#             perf | build | ci | test | revert
#   scope:    optional, lowercase, kebab-case (e.g. (auth), (linux-desktop))
#   subject:  imperative mood, lowercase, NO trailing period
#             "add foo" not "added foo" / "Adds foo." / "Add foo."
#   body:     explain motivation, side-effects, follow-ups
#   footer:   BREAKING CHANGE: <details>
#             Refs: #123, ABC-456
#             Co-Authored-By: Name <email>
#
# Mark a breaking change with `!` after type/scope, e.g.
#   refactor(api)!: drop /v1 endpoints
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
